<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hernán Siles Zuazo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1996</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hernán Siles Zuazo was a Bolivian politician, a founder of the Revolutionary Nationalist Movement (MNR) and a leader of the revolution of 1952. He was president from 1956 to 1960, when he imposed a stabilisation plan, and again from 1982 to 1985, when he restored democracy after years of military rule. His second government was overwhelmed by hyperinflation, and he called early elections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hernan-siles-zuazo.jpg" alt="Hernán Siles Zuazo" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luis Adolfo Gismondi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hern%C3%A1n_Siles_Zuazo3.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
